WEBVTT

00:35.637 --> 00:38.097
- Chris, did you get your homework done?
- Yup.

00:38.223 --> 00:40.141
Chris, I know
when you're lying to me.

00:40.224 --> 00:42.350
Just like Santa Claus knows
when you're sleeping.

00:43.518 --> 00:44.644
What was that?

00:44.769 --> 00:46.062
Hey, what the hell?

00:46.229 --> 00:47.438
Uh, hey.

00:48.647 --> 00:50.440
- Get out of here!
- Okay, okay!

00:50.565 --> 00:52.610
No, Mom. I got it all done.

00:52.734 --> 00:53.944
For my science homework,

00:54.026 --> 00:57.780
I had to make
a shoebox diarrhea of the evolution of man.

00:57.863 --> 00:59.447
You mean diorama?

01:00.573 --> 01:01.616
Uh-oh.

01:01.741 --> 01:03.534
Hey, Lois,
I got your pregnancy test.

01:03.659 --> 01:04.702
What the hell
you need this for?

01:04.827 --> 01:07.370
I need it
because I think I might be pregnant.

01:07.495 --> 01:09.955
What? My God,
are you sure it's yours?

01:10.039 --> 01:11.248
Lois pregnant?

01:11.331 --> 01:14.293
I didn't think the fat man still had that
kind of marksmanship.

01:14.376 --> 01:16.669
But that's what they said
about Lee Harvey Oswald.

01:17.213 --> 01:18.547
Hey, Mr. President!

01:18.671 --> 01:21.424
Mr. President, up here!
I voted for you!

01:21.548 --> 01:22.508
Wait a minute.

01:22.632 --> 01:24.718
That guy on the grassy knoll's
got a gun.

01:24.843 --> 01:26.178
He's gonna
shoot the President.

01:26.303 --> 01:28.180
Holy smokes,
I've got to do something.

01:28.429 --> 01:29.638
All right, Lee.

01:29.763 --> 01:32.222
Time to become
an American hero.

01:38.188 --> 01:41.106
Okay, one more minute,
and then if there are two pink lines...

01:41.190 --> 01:42.566
Oh, God, I hope
you're not pregnant.

01:42.690 --> 01:43.982
We can't afford another kid.

01:44.066 --> 01:45.860
We already got Chris,
Stewie, Richie,

01:45.985 --> 01:48.320
Joanie, Greg, Marcia,
Bobby, Jan,

01:48.403 --> 01:51.906
Mike Seaver, Carol Seaver,
Boner, Urkel, Mr. Furley...

01:52.031 --> 01:53.157
Peter, those aren't
your kids.

01:53.240 --> 01:54.326
<i>That's the
Nick at Nite lineup.</i>

01:54.409 --> 01:57.410
Blanka, Zangief,
Chun-Li, Guile, E. Honda...

01:57.536 --> 01:58.494
<i>That's Street Fighter.</i>

01:58.577 --> 01:59.579
Red, blue, green.

01:59.703 --> 02:01.038
Those are colors.

02:01.163 --> 02:03.665
God, I can't believe
we weren't more careful.

02:03.748 --> 02:06.543
This probably
happened that night we tried role-playing.

02:06.752 --> 02:09.002
Oh, I need a spanking.

02:09.086 --> 02:11.463
I'm a bad, bad girl.

02:11.546 --> 02:15.759
I'm a paladin
with 18 charisma and 97 hit points.

02:16.010 --> 02:19.970
I can use my helm
of disintegration and do one-D-four damage

02:20.054 --> 02:24.016
as my half-elf mage wields
his plus-five holy avenger.

02:24.100 --> 02:26.685
Paladins can't use
the helm of disintegration.

02:26.809 --> 02:29.936
Oh. Okay,
then I'm a black guy.

02:30.312 --> 02:31.939
Oh, thank God.
It's negative.

02:32.063 --> 02:35.024
Ooh. Dodged a bullet there, right?
Although, I got to tell you,

02:35.106 --> 02:36.817
I was kind of getting
used to the idea

02:36.901 --> 02:38.568
of having a little
brother or sister.

02:38.694 --> 02:41.029
Peter, we can't risk
these things anymore.

02:41.113 --> 02:42.448
You're absolutely right.

02:42.572 --> 02:44.074
Lois, you're getting
your tubes tied.

02:44.198 --> 02:45.823
Why should I
get my tubes tied?

02:45.907 --> 02:47.493
You should
get a vasectomy.

02:47.576 --> 02:49.244
First of all,
I don't know what that is,

02:49.369 --> 02:50.953
and, second of all,
no freaking way.

02:51.078 --> 02:52.413
Peter, it's the
male equivalent

02:52.539 --> 02:53.873
of a woman
getting her tubes tied,

02:53.956 --> 02:56.040
except, it's actually
a lot quicker and safer.

02:56.124 --> 02:57.374
Let these guys explain.

03:23.438 --> 03:26.065
Well, I'm starting
to get the picture, but how's it done?

04:46.379 --> 04:49.465
Lois, I know how to settle
our vasectomy dispute.

04:50.424 --> 04:53.843
A no-rules funny car race
from here to Boston.

04:53.968 --> 04:55.804
Last one to Fenway
gets snipped.

04:55.888 --> 04:57.180
Peter, what the hell?

04:57.305 --> 04:58.557
Where did these things
come from?

04:58.681 --> 05:00.682
They were Loretta's.
Please take them,

05:00.849 --> 05:02.892
they are no longer
funny to me.

05:03.100 --> 05:04.143
Go!

05:32.750 --> 05:35.751
Almost there.
Eat my dust, Lois.

05:57.644 --> 06:00.438
Well, it looks like
I'm a man with no sperm.

06:00.563 --> 06:03.107
But I'll always be a man
with no sperm

06:03.232 --> 06:05.651
who once had a wonderful day.

06:09.363 --> 06:11.406
Well, guys,
my vasectomy is tomorrow.

06:11.531 --> 06:12.989
You poor bastard.

06:13.073 --> 06:16.159
After all, sex is pointless
without potency.

06:16.242 --> 06:19.245
That's right. You take the venom
out of a cobra and what do you got?

06:19.370 --> 06:21.539
You got a, a belt.

06:21.621 --> 06:23.206
It's not that
big a deal.

06:23.332 --> 06:26.000
A bunch of the guys
on the force have had vasectomies,

06:26.083 --> 06:28.043
and their lives
haven't changed at all.

06:28.127 --> 06:29.462
Would you ever have one?

06:29.586 --> 06:31.045
Never!

06:32.882 --> 06:35.426
Well, yeah. But what if me and Lois
do end up wanting another baby?

06:35.551 --> 06:36.551
Lt'll be too late.

06:36.676 --> 06:38.177
You could freeze
some of your sperm

06:38.260 --> 06:40.052
at the sperm bank just in case.

06:40.136 --> 06:41.220
I don't know, Cleveland.

06:41.345 --> 06:43.473
It didn't work out so great
that time I froze my nuts.

06:45.809 --> 06:48.018
No! No! Bad squirrel.

06:49.184 --> 06:51.687
Those are my nuts. My nuts!

06:51.769 --> 06:54.231
You're just
a hungry little fellow, aren't you?

06:54.314 --> 06:56.066
But those are my nuts!

06:57.233 --> 06:59.402
No. Oh, God, no!
My nuts! My nuts!

07:02.946 --> 07:04.655
- Hey, Brian. You want to play tag?
- No.

07:04.781 --> 07:05.782
- Freeze tag?
- No.

07:05.907 --> 07:06.867
- TV tag?
- No.

07:06.992 --> 07:08.993
If I can get some guys
you want to play Red Rover?

07:09.118 --> 07:10.661
No. Maybe.
You get the guys first.

07:10.787 --> 07:12.413
We'll talk about it.

07:13.788 --> 07:15.831
No! Jungle gym mine!

07:15.957 --> 07:18.124
Hey, where'd you get
the Pete Rose haircut?

07:20.835 --> 07:24.088
Anyone else want to feel
my Weebok in their grapes?

07:24.881 --> 07:26.882
Then you'll all do as I say.

07:26.965 --> 07:29.051
- Hi.
- Well, hello there.

07:30.218 --> 07:31.928
Yes, that's right, cry.

07:32.053 --> 07:34.638
Cry like Sauron when he lost
his contact lens.

07:34.764 --> 07:36.640
Nobody move! Nobody move!

07:36.765 --> 07:38.267
Does anybody see it?

07:38.392 --> 07:40.143
It might be stuck
to a tree or a rock.

07:40.267 --> 07:41.435
Anyone?

07:41.518 --> 07:43.438
Oh, I am so grounded.

07:45.940 --> 07:48.567
Hi, there. Peter Griffin.
I've got an appointment

07:48.651 --> 07:51.652
to, uh, banish a White Russian
from my Kremlin.

07:51.735 --> 07:54.779
Well, we don't have empty rooms
right now, but if you'll have a seat...

07:54.862 --> 07:57.489
Yeah. I kind of
warmed myself up

07:57.615 --> 07:59.159
in the car
if you catch my drift.

07:59.284 --> 08:02.161
- I could put you in the storage freezer.
- That'll work.

08:02.994 --> 08:05.245
Nurse, I've got a splinter.

08:06.331 --> 08:08.123
Just come out
whenever you're done.

08:09.500 --> 08:13.294
Oh, God! Oh, God! Oh, God!

08:15.046 --> 08:16.505
Oh, God! I...

08:16.755 --> 08:18.799
I think I feel them moving.

08:18.924 --> 08:21.635
Hi. My partner and I
want to have a baby.

08:21.717 --> 08:23.219
We'd like a vial of sperm

08:23.344 --> 08:26.597
and an applicator
that looks like Jodie Foster's knuckles.

08:26.681 --> 08:29.474
Certainly. Let me
just go to the freezer.

08:30.726 --> 08:33.436
Mr. Griffin,
you were in there an awfully long time.

08:33.519 --> 08:35.771
- Are you all right?
- Yup, yup. Fine, fine.

08:35.855 --> 08:37.815
And just so you know,
everything in there

08:37.897 --> 08:39.815
is exactly the way
it was when I went in.

08:39.899 --> 08:43.151
There is absolutely
zero chance that I spilled all the jars

08:43.276 --> 08:44.736
and had to refill them
with my own sperm.

08:44.861 --> 08:45.820
Zero chance.

08:54.161 --> 08:55.495
It's a boy!

08:57.371 --> 09:00.206
Victory shall be mine!

09:08.087 --> 09:12.634
<i>We now return to Tony Danza
and Sylvester Stallone in What?</i>

09:26.394 --> 09:27.854
Peter, we have to talk.

09:27.980 --> 09:30.272
We haven't had sex
since your vasectomy.

09:30.397 --> 09:32.024
Yeah, I just don't
feel like it, Lois,

09:32.149 --> 09:34.191
seeing as how I'm
not a real man anymore.

09:34.275 --> 09:36.694
Honey, it was just
a simple operation.

09:36.777 --> 09:39.072
It's no reason to
give up on your sex life.

09:39.196 --> 09:41.615
I don't know, Lois.
I'm just not feeling it anymore.

09:41.740 --> 09:43.867
Besides, it gives me time
to try new things,

09:43.992 --> 09:46.035
like that time I tried
wearing adult diapers.

09:46.452 --> 09:47.745
Hey, Lois. Hey, kids.

09:47.870 --> 09:49.414
Oh, boy,
that smells delicious.

09:49.538 --> 09:51.289
You know, I'd love to stay
and eat with you,

09:51.415 --> 09:54.584
but I got to go meet
Cleveland, Joe, and Quagmire down at...

09:57.086 --> 09:58.879
the bar.
So just put my dinner

09:58.962 --> 10:00.713
in the fridge
and I'll heat it up later.

10:00.839 --> 10:01.881
Love you.

10:05.217 --> 10:06.551
You, go get me an ice cream.

10:06.676 --> 10:07.678
You, clear the slide.

10:07.762 --> 10:08.970
I'm going down
in five minutes.

10:09.095 --> 10:11.556
You! Did you get me
my Cheez Whiz, boy?

10:12.598 --> 10:13.891
You're my boyfriend.

10:14.058 --> 10:15.351
Yes, dear. Of course I am.

10:15.435 --> 10:17.352
Now, where's Lloyd
with our Fun Dip?

10:17.434 --> 10:20.396
Good God! Running an empire
is harder than finding diversity

10:20.479 --> 10:22.565
in the Abercrombie & Fitch catalog.

10:26.692 --> 10:28.236
Ooh! Ooh! There he is.
There he is. Right there.

10:28.320 --> 10:29.318
Ah, found him.

10:29.444 --> 10:30.988
That was a tricky one.

10:32.196 --> 10:33.448
No kidding. He looks weird.

10:33.573 --> 10:36.075
What the deuce is
all the commotion?

10:36.159 --> 10:37.869
All right.
Out of my way. Move aside.

10:37.951 --> 10:40.662
What the hell is so
bloody fascinating?

10:40.788 --> 10:42.287
You!

10:42.412 --> 10:43.789
Well, well, well.

10:43.998 --> 10:46.416
If it isn't my
half brother Stewie!

10:46.500 --> 10:49.711
Bertram! I haven't
seen you since our microscopic encounter.

10:49.795 --> 10:51.880
How the deuce
did you get out of Peter's testicles?

10:51.964 --> 10:53.590
- He donated sperm.
- Gross.

10:53.673 --> 10:55.256
Well, I don't mean
to be a discourteous host,

10:55.340 --> 10:56.883
but this is my playground.

10:56.966 --> 10:58.259
I rule this territory.

10:58.342 --> 11:00.802
My, my! What an amusingly
misguided view.

11:00.886 --> 11:05.057
Very well, then. You leave me
no choice but to declare war!

11:05.141 --> 11:09.351
<i>So be it. I'll do to you
what B.C. does to comedy on a daily basis.</i>

11:09.476 --> 11:11.436
<i>Hey, why is Juan so happy?</i>

11:11.520 --> 11:13.938
<i>I think he finally figured himself out.</i>

11:14.022 --> 11:17.067
<i>Huh, I guess it takes Juan to know Juan.</i>

11:21.986 --> 11:23.946
Hey, boys. You having
a midnight snack?

11:24.071 --> 11:25.031
- Hmm.
- Mmm-hmm.

11:25.156 --> 11:27.617
I'm just gonna
grab something, too, and go back to bed

11:27.741 --> 11:29.701
alone again.

11:30.119 --> 11:31.244
Night.

11:32.035 --> 11:33.746
You know, Lois
has gotten kind of fat

11:33.830 --> 11:35.456
since you guys
stopped having sex.

11:35.581 --> 11:39.293
It might be
time to, you know, have some sex.

11:39.419 --> 11:41.921
You know, at first I didn't want to do it
'cause of the vasectomy.

11:42.004 --> 11:44.338
But now it's just...
I mean, look at her.

11:44.463 --> 11:46.298
She's got elbow cleavage.

11:46.423 --> 11:49.342
You know, that little wrinkle
that fat people get on their elbows

11:49.467 --> 11:50.551
that looks like a schwa?

11:50.676 --> 11:52.637
I mean, you wouldn't have
sex with her, would you?

11:52.761 --> 11:54.138
- Oh, yeah, I would.
- Really?

11:54.222 --> 11:56.180
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.
I would do everything to her.

11:56.264 --> 11:57.599
I don't care
what she looks like.

11:57.683 --> 11:59.099
I would wreck that chick.

11:59.183 --> 12:00.601
Well, you are a trouper.

12:03.603 --> 12:05.272
Sorry. Fat wife
coming through.

12:05.356 --> 12:07.815
Sorry. Sorry.
Excuse me. Fat wife.

12:07.898 --> 12:09.232
Oh, hold on a sec.

12:12.444 --> 12:13.612
All right, bring her through.

12:13.695 --> 12:14.820
Peter, stop it.

12:14.946 --> 12:17.156
For God's sake,
you're embarrassing me.

12:17.240 --> 12:18.491
Not as embarrassed
as I was

12:18.575 --> 12:20.825
when I got that job
entertaining prison inmates.

12:20.950 --> 12:22.201
Do it again, Griffin.

12:22.326 --> 12:24.120
Come on. I just did it,
like, five times.

12:24.202 --> 12:25.412
Do it!

12:35.837 --> 12:37.422
Look, honey,
with all due respect,

12:37.546 --> 12:39.048
you've gained
some weight recently.

12:39.174 --> 12:40.633
It's five pounds at the most.

12:40.717 --> 12:41.843
It's not a big deal.

12:41.968 --> 12:45.469
It's a slippery slope, Lois. You start with
five pounds and then one day, boom!

12:45.552 --> 12:48.681
<i>You wake up and you're on The Practice
with 16 rings in your ear.</i>

12:48.806 --> 12:51.016
You're one to talk.
Look how fat you are.

12:51.100 --> 12:52.393
Lois, men aren't fat.

12:52.518 --> 12:54.102
Only fat women are fat.

12:54.227 --> 12:57.396
Now, if you'll excuse me, I have to go
warn the chef that you've arrived.

12:59.231 --> 13:01.566
He wants fat?
I'll show him fat.

13:01.691 --> 13:04.193
The only reason
I'm eating anyway is because of him.

13:04.277 --> 13:05.903
He won't touch me.

13:07.905 --> 13:09.196
Do you think I'm fat?

13:09.322 --> 13:10.573
Only if you think
I'm a serial killer.

13:10.699 --> 13:11.656
- What?
- Nothing.

13:13.075 --> 13:14.326
Attention, all hands.

13:14.409 --> 13:16.204
We're going to launch
a massive air strike

13:16.287 --> 13:17.663
against Bertram
and his army.

13:17.746 --> 13:19.414
Behold the armada.

13:23.083 --> 13:24.376
It's quite simple, actually.

13:24.459 --> 13:26.211
You press the smiling duck
to take off,

13:26.294 --> 13:28.629
the cow with the bow
tie to fire weapons,

13:28.755 --> 13:31.716
and the clown face
is just a clown face. Enjoy it.

13:31.800 --> 13:34.050
Now, battle stations,
everyone!

13:35.134 --> 13:38.596
At my signal, unleash hell!

13:53.108 --> 13:54.693
What took you so long?

13:54.776 --> 13:56.652
What took you so ugly?

14:44.315 --> 14:45.275
Well, now what?

14:45.401 --> 14:46.774
- You want to play 20 questions?
- Sure.

14:46.858 --> 14:48.276
- Uh, is it a man?
- Yes.

14:48.359 --> 14:49.402
- Is he famous?
- Yes.

14:49.485 --> 14:50.529
- Is he under 40?
- No.

14:50.654 --> 14:51.654
- Over 40?
- Yes.

14:51.779 --> 14:52.738
- On television?
- Yes.

14:52.864 --> 14:53.905
- On television now?
- No.

14:53.989 --> 14:55.282
- In the past 20 years?
- Yes.

14:55.366 --> 14:56.909
- Is it Richard Mulligan?
- Yes!

14:57.910 --> 15:00.661
Up until now,
we've been fighting Bertram on his terms.

15:00.787 --> 15:03.163
Whoa, easy.
Easy, girl. Easy, easy, easy.

15:03.289 --> 15:04.706
But I propose an invasion.

15:04.832 --> 15:06.832
We've got to
fight him over there by the swing set

15:06.957 --> 15:09.044
so we don't have to
fight him here at the sandbox.

15:09.169 --> 15:10.128
Stewie?

15:10.212 --> 15:11.211
What's this?

15:13.004 --> 15:15.131
A letter of surrender.
We did it.

15:15.256 --> 15:16.966
Whew! It's a good thing,
too, because

15:17.091 --> 15:18.759
I really didn't
have an exit strategy.

15:18.843 --> 15:20.177
Yay, Stewie!

15:20.302 --> 15:22.055
Oh, thank you, darling. I...

15:22.263 --> 15:23.512
What is this? Makeup?

15:23.638 --> 15:25.097
Why are you wearing makeup?

15:25.180 --> 15:27.309
Chicken pox!

15:31.186 --> 15:34.522
Damn you, Bertram.
I thought we called no biological warfare.

15:34.647 --> 15:36.315
You swore on the seesaw.

15:40.984 --> 15:42.654
Stewie, there you are.

15:42.737 --> 15:44.614
Oh, my God. Your face.

15:44.697 --> 15:46.866
Oh, sweetie.
You got the chicken pox.

15:46.990 --> 15:48.616
Come on, we got to
get you out of here.

15:48.699 --> 15:51.327
No. No, damn you,
I've got to finish what I've started!

15:51.451 --> 15:53.787
No... My God,
you've put on weight.

15:53.870 --> 15:56.498
You're like one of those
Memory Foam mattresses.

15:56.581 --> 15:58.417
Look, there's my face.

16:04.129 --> 16:05.505
Here you go, sweetie.

16:05.588 --> 16:08.299
A couple of more oatmeal baths
and you'll be all better.

16:08.382 --> 16:10.050
Well, no need to clean up
when I'm done.

16:10.175 --> 16:12.176
You'll probably just
slice a couple of bananas in here

16:12.300 --> 16:14.346
and chow down, huh, porky?

16:14.471 --> 16:16.346
So what happened
with that kid on the playground?

16:16.430 --> 16:17.514
He won this round, Brian.

16:17.639 --> 16:18.848
But I'm going back tomorrow.

16:18.932 --> 16:21.517
And when I've carried out my plan,
he won't know what hit him,

16:21.601 --> 16:23.436
like that baseball team
that Peter coached.

16:23.562 --> 16:25.104
Well, kids,
just when I thought

16:25.228 --> 16:26.855
we'd never find
an assistant coach,

16:26.938 --> 16:28.356
I ran into this drifter
hanging out

16:28.439 --> 16:30.192
near the elementary
school playground.

16:30.317 --> 16:31.776
He's got a clown costume
in his trunk,

16:31.901 --> 16:33.318
so we know
he's good with kids,

16:33.402 --> 16:35.530
and pictures of boys
in their underwear, so

16:35.655 --> 16:37.279
he's probably had
some medical training.

16:37.405 --> 16:39.282
Well, I'm gonna take off
while he fits you

16:39.406 --> 16:41.199
for cups in that
windowless supply shed.

16:41.324 --> 16:42.534
See you.

16:45.161 --> 16:47.497
<i>This Friday on TNT, the world premiere</i>

16:47.581 --> 16:49.873
<i>of Morgan Freeman
in The Narrator.</i>

16:49.956 --> 16:52.125
<i>Ever since I was a little boy,</i>

16:52.251 --> 16:54.711
<i>people have enjoyed
the sound of my voice.</i>

16:54.836 --> 16:57.547
<i>And I figured
you either get busy talking</i>

16:57.631 --> 16:59.506
<i>or you get busy dying.</i>

16:59.589 --> 17:01.550
<i>The work is really quite easy.</i>

17:01.634 --> 17:04.593
<i>Why, even right now,
I'm just sitting in a chair</i>

17:04.677 --> 17:07.470
<i>sipping some tea
and reading from a script.</i>

17:07.596 --> 17:11.474
<i>The wall is covered
with something that resembles egg crates,</i>

17:11.600 --> 17:15.018
<i>except they're
soft and spongy like a Twinkie.</i>

17:15.393 --> 17:16.895
<i>Like a Twinkie.</i>

17:17.021 --> 17:20.189
Oh, hey, Hogzilla. You happen to see
my hot wife Lois around?

17:20.273 --> 17:21.441
No, I haven't.

17:21.566 --> 17:24.277
Maybe she's out
looking for a man who can satisfy her.

17:24.401 --> 17:26.694
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
Do me a favor.

17:26.778 --> 17:28.779
When you go to sleep,
aim your butt the other way.

17:28.863 --> 17:30.323
Last night, for God's sake,
you farted.

17:30.448 --> 17:31.490
I felt like somebody
was sticking me

17:31.616 --> 17:33.408
with a cigarette lighter
from the car.

17:33.533 --> 17:35.786
- You're fat.
- Shut up and go to sleep!

17:37.329 --> 17:39.162
Lois, you weigh a ton!
Get off me!

17:39.288 --> 17:41.081
- I'm trying, I...
- Try harder!

17:41.206 --> 17:44.959
- Peter, if you just stop for one second...
- Lois, that hurts. Quit it.

17:49.088 --> 17:50.671
Peter, are we having sex?

17:50.797 --> 17:53.884
Let's check.
Just lift up that fold right there.

17:54.009 --> 17:55.092
Uh, yup.

17:58.804 --> 18:00.931
Lois, last night
was amazing.

18:01.055 --> 18:02.388
It was, wasn't it?

18:02.472 --> 18:05.308
Fat sex
is the hottest sex we've ever had.

18:05.434 --> 18:08.061
There were so many boobs,
I didn't know whose boobs I was grabbing,

18:08.145 --> 18:09.563
your boobs or my boobs.

18:09.647 --> 18:11.398
I know. It was amazing.

18:11.481 --> 18:14.900
Much better than that night you pretended
your penis was Danny Aiello.

18:14.983 --> 18:18.986
Oh, that is so interesting,
Danny Aiello.

18:19.111 --> 18:21.572
You've got the best
Spike Lee stories.

18:21.697 --> 18:24.075
What's that?
You want to meet my wife?

18:24.157 --> 18:25.452
Peter, stop it.

18:25.534 --> 18:26.743
Lois, just say hello.

18:26.825 --> 18:29.370
You're embarrassing me
in front of Danny Aiello.

18:29.494 --> 18:32.331
Now, come here,
my fat concubine.

18:32.455 --> 18:34.416
Hey, I'm not even hungry.

18:34.499 --> 18:36.584
I want you bigger.
I want you fatter.

18:36.667 --> 18:38.044
It will please me.

18:42.464 --> 18:43.632
With Stewart out of the picture,

18:43.715 --> 18:47.175
this whole playground
is under my control.

19:02.729 --> 19:04.356
I sense something.

19:04.481 --> 19:06.816
A presence
I've not felt since...

19:08.734 --> 19:10.235
Stewie, you're alive.

19:10.361 --> 19:11.904
Yes, Bertram, I'm alive.

19:12.029 --> 19:14.949
And I think you'll find
all your guards quite incapacitated.

19:15.033 --> 19:18.951
You have an annoying habit
of turning up where you're not welcome.

19:19.035 --> 19:21.035
Well, when I'm done with you,
you're going to hate me more

19:21.161 --> 19:23.039
than the other vowels hate "Y."

19:23.289 --> 19:25.499
If you'll turn to Page 34
of your blue books,

19:25.624 --> 19:27.417
you'll see our projections
for next quarter,

19:27.541 --> 19:29.501
- which I can tell are...
- Okay, okay. Yeah, all right.

19:29.585 --> 19:31.460
You know what?
I'm in a meeting. I'll call you back.

19:31.543 --> 19:34.338
Well, well, well.
Look who decided to show up.

19:34.463 --> 19:36.631
- So, what are we talking about here?
- Well, before you...

19:37.842 --> 19:40.011
Oh, I'm sorry. F, what's up?

19:40.134 --> 19:41.511
No, no. I can talk.

19:41.594 --> 19:42.679
En garde!

20:39.682 --> 20:41.101
Any last words?

20:41.184 --> 20:43.518
You wouldn't kill me,
would you?

20:44.894 --> 20:47.438
Thanks for helping me
dig this hole, Mr. Montesante.

20:47.563 --> 20:49.023
Hey, no problem, Stewie.

20:49.149 --> 20:52.276
This can be a pain in the ass
when you got to do it all by yourself.

20:52.401 --> 20:55.778
You're telling me.
All right. Go ahead and drop it in.

20:55.903 --> 20:58.656
Oh, boy. That's gonna be beautiful
when it reaches adulthood.

20:58.781 --> 21:00.323
Yeah. I love plants.

21:00.448 --> 21:02.535
So what happened with that kid
you were telling me about?

21:02.619 --> 21:04.161
He admitted defeat
and ran off.

21:04.286 --> 21:05.412
What a mook!

21:08.163 --> 21:10.706
Oh, Peter,
I love you so much.

21:11.874 --> 21:14.168
Oh, Lois. I have
no idea if we're doing it

21:14.294 --> 21:15.753
or if that's just
the back of your knee,

21:15.879 --> 21:18.255
but either way,
it feels so good.

21:18.338 --> 21:21.464
Oh, Peter,
you're on my arm. It hurts.

21:21.590 --> 21:23.552
Oh! My chest hurts, too.

21:23.634 --> 21:25.010
Oh, my God.

21:25.135 --> 21:27.637
Peter, I think
I'm having a heart attack.

21:27.763 --> 21:29.388
Oh, me, too, sweetie.
Me, too.

21:29.472 --> 21:31.765
No, no, Peter, I'm really
having a heart attack.

21:31.848 --> 21:33.350
Oh, my God!
You're serious?

21:33.475 --> 21:34.558
Oh, we should get you
to the hospital.

21:34.642 --> 21:35.810
All right,
hold-hold on a sec.

21:35.935 --> 21:38.104
- I... All right, almost done. Almost done.
- Peter!

21:38.187 --> 21:40.731
Almost done. Almost done.
Almost done. Okay, let's go.

21:42.648 --> 21:44.942
Well, it was a tough job
removing all that fat

21:45.025 --> 21:46.360
to get to your heart,
Mrs. Griffin.

21:46.485 --> 21:47.945
But you came
through it beautifully.

21:48.028 --> 21:50.948
Honey, I'm sorry I tried
to make you into something you're not.

21:51.032 --> 21:53.492
I love you no matter
what size you are.

21:53.575 --> 21:54.660
Although, I got to admit,

21:54.784 --> 21:57.994
I'm gonna miss eating cereal out of
the dimples on your ass.

21:58.119 --> 21:59.454
Well, Mrs. Griffin,
you rest up

21:59.537 --> 22:01.540
for a few days
and you'll be just fine.

22:01.664 --> 22:02.791
Thank you, Doctor.

22:02.916 --> 22:06.210
I realize now that eating is not the way
to solve my problems.

22:06.335 --> 22:07.418
You hear that, Meg?

22:07.502 --> 22:10.797
For your information, Mom,
I don't eat to solve my problems.

22:10.880 --> 22:13.424
I cut myself.
Is that better?

22:13.508 --> 22:15.885
Chris, we all love your hat.

22:16.010 --> 22:17.302
Thanks, Mom.

22:17.427 --> 22:20.304
Hey, Doc, what did you do
with my mom's fat?

22:20.429 --> 22:22.723
Oh, it's right here
in this storage closet.

22:23.808 --> 22:24.766
Uh...

22:25.350 --> 22:27.310
It's exactly
what it looks like.

22:27.311 --> 24:28.311
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru